## 🐧 Section 7: Universal Real-Time Linux (`6.12-rt` / Buildroot / Desktop) Setup

This hardened configuration works identically across **bare-metal Buildroot/Batocera (`Piccolo [AX]`)** (SysVinit/eudev without systemd or WirePlumber) and **desktop Linux (`Ubuntu/Kubuntu 24.04+` or `piccolo-ax-desktop`)** (systemd + WirePlumber `0.5+`). It removes deprecated `nrpacks=1` kernel warnings, locks USB autosuspend off, prevents desktop audio servers from claiming the DAC, and uses group-safe runtime PID tracking with kernel ALSA subdevice drain checks.

### 1. Universal `udev` Rules & Real-Time Limits

Save this to `/etc/udev/rules.d/99-hiby-fc3-ax.rules` to grant the `audio` group `0660` ownership over both `/dev/snd/*` and raw USB nodes while locking USB autosuspend off (`power/control="on"`):

```udev
# /etc/udev/rules.d/99-hiby-fc3-ax.rules
# 1. Prevent PulseAudio / legacy PipeWire ACP from claiming HiBy FC3 (VID 0x32BB)
SUBSYSTEM=="sound", ATTRS{idVendor}=="32bb", ENV{PULSE_IGNORE}="1", ENV{ACP_IGNORE}="1", GROUP="audio", MODE="0660"

# 2. Disable USB autosuspend and grant audio group raw USB access
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="32bb", MODE="0660", GROUP="audio", TEST=="power/control", ATTR{power/control}="on", TEST=="power/autosuspend", ATTR{power/autosuspend}="-1"
```

Remove any legacy `nrpacks=1` modprobe file (modern `6.12+` `snd-usb-audio` handles USB isochronous packet framing dynamically):

```bash
sudo rm -f /etc/modprobe.d/hiby-fc3-ax.conf
```

Configure real-time scheduling and unlimited locked RAM in `/etc/security/limits.d/99-flac-ax.conf` (for PAM-enabled desktops; bare-metal Buildroot/Batocera processes inherit RT privileges directly):

```conf
# /etc/security/limits.d/99-flac-ax.conf
@audio   -  rtprio     95
@audio   -  memlock    unlimited
@audio   -  nice      -19
```

Apply and verify:

```bash
sudo usermod -aG audio "$USER"
sudo udevadm control --reload-rules && sudo udevadm trigger

# Replug HiBy FC3 and verify USB autosuspend is locked "on" and group is "audio":
grep -l "32bb" /sys/bus/usb/devices/*/idVendor | xargs -I{} dirname {} | xargs -I{} cat {}/power/control
ls -l /dev/snd/pcmC*
```

### 2. WirePlumber `0.5+` Device Exclusion Rule (Desktop Linux Only)

If PipeWire/WirePlumber is installed (`Ubuntu/Kubuntu` or `piccolo-ax-desktop`), block WirePlumber from opening `hw:CARD=FC3,DEV=0` by creating `/etc/wireplumber/wireplumber.conf.d/51-ignore-hiby-fc3.conf` *(skip this step on bare-metal Buildroot/Batocera)*:

```hocon
# /etc/wireplumber/wireplumber.conf.d/51-ignore-hiby-fc3.conf
monitor.alsa.rules = [
  {
    matches = [
      {
        device.vendor.id = "0x32bb"
      }
    ]
    actions = {
      update-props = {
        device.disabled = true
      }
    }
  }
]
```

Restart and verify WirePlumber no longer holds the device:

```bash
systemctl --user restart wireplumber
wpctl status          # HiBy FC3 must NOT appear under Audio Devices
fuser -v /dev/snd/*   # Must return empty for the FC3 card node
```

### 3. Universal Launcher & Switcher (`~/bin/ax-launch.sh`)

Uses `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` on systemd desktops or a `0770` `/tmp/ax-runtime` directory on Buildroot/Batocera, validates paths and volume bounds before interrupting active playback, and polls `/proc/asound/cardX/pcm0p/sub0/status` until closed to eliminate ALSA `EBUSY` collisions:

```bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash
# ~/bin/ax-launch.sh — Deterministic Core 0 launcher for HiBy FC3 (Buildroot & Desktop Linux)
set -euo pipefail

# Use systemd XDG_RUNTIME_DIR if available; otherwise create a group-shared dir in /tmp
if [[ -n "${XDG_RUNTIME_DIR:-}" && -d "$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR" ]]; then
    RUNTIME_DIR="$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR"
else
    RUNTIME_DIR="/tmp/ax-runtime"
    mkdir -p "$RUNTIME_DIR"
    chmod 0770 "$RUNTIME_DIR" 2>/dev/null || true
fi

PIDFILE="${RUNTIME_DIR}/ax-dac.pid"
DEVICE="hw:CARD=FC3,DEV=0"
CARD_NAME="FC3"

MODE="${1:-music}"
VOL="${2:-0.80}"
TARGET="${3:-}"

usage() {
    echo "Usage: $0 {music|synth|retro|dvd} [volume: 0.01-1.00] [album_dir_or_iso]" >&2
    exit 1
}

# 1. Validate arguments BEFORE tearing down any active audio engine
case "$MODE" in
    music|dvd)
        [[ -z "$TARGET" || ! -e "$TARGET" ]] && { echo "Error: Missing or invalid target path for $MODE." >&2; usage; }
        ;;
    synth|retro)
        ;;
    *)
        usage
        ;;
esac

if ! awk -v v="$VOL" 'BEGIN { exit !(v > 0.0 && v <= 1.0) }'; then
    echo "Error: Volume '$VOL' out of safe range (0.01 - 1.00)." >&2
    exit 1
fi

# 2. Verify DAC presence before proceeding
if ! grep -q "\[$CARD_NAME" /proc/asound/cards 2>/dev/null; then
    echo "Error: HiBy FC3 ($DEVICE) not detected in /proc/asound/cards." >&2
    exit 1
fi

# 3. Cleanly terminate previous engine and wait for ALSA PCM release
if [[ -f "$PIDFILE" ]]; then
    OLD_PID=$(cat "$PIDFILE" 2>/dev/null || true)
    if [[ -n "$OLD_PID" ]] && kill -0 "$OLD_PID" 2>/dev/null; then
        kill -TERM "$OLD_PID" 2>/dev/null || true
        for _ in {1..100}; do
            kill -0 "$OLD_PID" 2>/dev/null || break
            sleep 0.01
        done
        if kill -0 "$OLD_PID" 2>/dev/null; then
            kill -KILL "$OLD_PID" 2>/dev/null || true
        fi
    fi
    rm -f "$PIDFILE"
fi

# Ensure kernel ALSA PCM subdevice is closed (avoids EBUSY on fast switch)
CARD_NUM=$(awk -F'[][]' "/\[$CARD_NAME/ {print \$1}" /proc/asound/cards | tr -d ' ')
if [[ -n "$CARD_NUM" && -f "/proc/asound/card${CARD_NUM}/pcm0p/sub0/status" ]]; then
    for _ in {1..50}; do
        grep -q "closed" "/proc/asound/card${CARD_NUM}/pcm0p/sub0/status" && break
        sleep 0.01
    done
fi

# 4. Cleanup trap to prevent stale PID files on exit
CHILD_PID=""
cleanup() {
    if [[ -n "$CHILD_PID" ]] && kill -0 "$CHILD_PID" 2>/dev/null; then
        kill -TERM "$CHILD_PID" 2>/dev/null || true
        wait "$CHILD_PID" 2>/dev/null || true
    fi
    rm -f "$PIDFILE"
}
trap cleanup EXIT INT TERM

# 5. Launch requested engine pinned to Core 0 (SCHED_FIFO 80)
CMD=()
case "$MODE" in
    music)
        CMD=(flac_ax --device "$DEVICE" --volume "$VOL" "$TARGET")
        ;;
    synth)
        CMD=(ax_av_studio --device "$DEVICE" --volume "$VOL")
        ;;
    retro)
        CMD=(ax_video_upscaler --mode retro --preset 1080p --device "$DEVICE" --volume "$VOL")
        ;;
    dvd)
        CMD=(ax_video_upscaler --mode dvd --preset 2k --device "$DEVICE" --volume "$VOL" "$TARGET")
        ;;
esac

chrt -f 80 taskset -c 0 "${CMD[@]}" &
CHILD_PID=$!
echo "$CHILD_PID" > "$PIDFILE"
wait "$CHILD_PID"
```

Make executable and verify real-time pinning (`CLS=FF`, `RTPRIO=80`, `PSR=0`):

```bash
chmod +x ~/bin/ax-launch.sh

# Example 1: Speakers (TPA3116/TPA3255) or Sennheiser HD 560S (120 Ohm)
~/bin/ax-launch.sh music 0.80 ~/Music/FLAC_Album/

# Example 2: Sensitive 16-18 Ohm IEMs/headphones (Moondrop Chu II/III, Sennheiser HD400S)
~/bin/ax-launch.sh music 0.25 ~/Music/FLAC_Album/

# Example 3: Instant handoff to 2.00 ms synth workstation & verify Core 0 SCHED_FIFO 80
