## 🪟 Section 8: Windows 10/11 Fallback Setup (If Dual-Booting)

If you boot into Windows 10/11 on the same machine, apply these settings to maintain `~1–3 ms` analog hardware latency and avoid OS DSP degradation:

1. **Disable Audio Enhancements:** Open *Sound Settings → Device Properties → Additional Device Properties → Enhancements* and check **Disable all enhancements** (and turn off Windows Sonic / Spatial Sound) to cut `~20–30 ms` of OS buffer delay.
2. **Match Sample Rate / Use WASAPI Exclusive:** Under the *Advanced* tab, set default format to **24-bit, 44100 Hz** (music) or **24-bit, 48000 Hz** (gaming/movies), or enable **WASAPI Exclusive Mode** in Foobar2000/MusicBee for bit-perfect output.
3. **Gain Staging:** Keep Windows volume at **100%** when feeding your `TPA3116`/`TPA3255` speaker amp and adjust volume via the physical amp dial; drop Windows volume to **20–30%** before plugging in sensitive `16–18 Ω` IEMs/headphones (Moondrop Chu II/III, Sennheiser HD400S).
